<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theobald Bourke, 1st Viscount Mayo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1567–<a href="/years/1629">1629</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Tibbot na Long</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theobald Bourke, known as Tibbot na Long ('of the ships'), was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grace-omalley">Grace O'Malley</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-an-iarainn-bourke">Richard an Iarainn Bourke</a>, said to have been born at sea. He grew up as a Mayo lord and at first fought the English, but sided with the Crown during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland">Nine Years' War</a>, including at Kinsale in 1601. He was knighted and in 1627 created Viscount Mayo by Charles I.</p></div>
